      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>How the Creator Stack Calculator works</h2>
        <p>
          Creator income can pass through several separate deductions before it
          reaches your bank account. This calculator keeps platform fees,
          payment processing fees and foreign-exchange costs separate.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Platform fees:</strong> deductions applied before the payout route when your entered amount is a contract or gross amount.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment processing:</strong> fees charged by the payment provider or payout route.</li>
          <li><strong>FX cost:</strong> the difference between the reference exchange rate and the rate after your entered markup.</li>
          <li><strong>Estimated take-home:</strong> the amount remaining after the modeled deductions and any optional planning reserve.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If an amount is already after platform fees, select that stage. If it
          has already reached your account, select “Already received” so the
          calculator does not deduct payout fees or convert it again.
        </p>
      </section>

