        <details>
          <summary>What is the Creator Stack Calculator?</summary>
          <p>
            It is a calculator for bringing multiple creator and freelance
            income sources into one combined estimate, while modeling
            applicable platform deductions, payment costs and FX impact
            from the information you provide.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I combine YouTube and freelance income?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. You can enter different income sources in the same
            calculation. Make sure you select the correct income stage
            for each source so deductions are not counted twice.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I add income from multiple platforms?</summary>
          <p>
            The calculator is designed to model multiple income sources.
            Add each source separately and provide its relevant income,
            currency and fee information.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Does the calculator automatically know every platform fee?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Do not assume a fee is verified unless the calculator
            explicitly identifies it as verified. Where a fee is not
            verified, enter the applicable fee yourself rather than
            relying on an assumed default.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What if I do not know my payment provider's fee?</summary>
          <p>
            Check the provider's current pricing or transaction statement
            before entering a fee. An unknown fee should not be treated
            as a confirmed zero-cost payout.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What is the difference between gross income and estimated take-home?</summary>
          <p>
            Gross income is the amount before the deductions that apply
            at the selected income stage. Estimated take-home is the
            modeled amount remaining after the applicable deductions
            and any optional planning reserve entered into the calculator.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How does currency conversion affect my income?</summary>
          <p>
            When income is converted into another currency, the exchange
            rate and any entered FX markup affect the converted amount.
            Your bank or provider may apply a different rate or additional
            charges.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I enter income after platform fees have already been deducted?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Select the after-platform-fees income stage where
            applicable. This helps prevent the same platform deduction
            from being applied again.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I enter money that has already reached my account?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Use the Already received stage when the amount has
            already reached your account. The calculator should not
            deduct payout fees or convert that amount again.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Does this calculator tell me how much tax I owe?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Any optional reserve is an amount you choose for planning.
            It is not a calculation of your actual tax liability.
            Consult a qualified tax professional for advice about your
            circumstances.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Will the estimated result exactly match my bank payout?</summary>
          <p>
            Not necessarily. Actual payouts can differ because of provider
            pricing, exchange-rate spreads, timing, intermediary charges
            and other transaction-specific adjustments.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Is the Creator Stack Calculator free?</summary>
